---
import { pageDates } from "../page-dates.js";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site.config.js";
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles data: what the site stores, how advertising cookies from Google and its partners work, and how to opt out.`}
  updated={pageDates("/privacy/").updated ?? pageDates("/privacy/").published}
>
  <p>This policy explains what information {SITE.name} ({SITE.domain}) collects, how it is used and the choices you have. If you have questions, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>You don't need an account to use {SITE.name}. Every quiz runs entirely in your browser. Your clicks and answers are not sent to our servers. If you play today's quiz, that day's answers are saved in your browser's local storage so you can see it when you come back; it never leaves your device. Your light or dark theme choice is saved in your browser only.</p>

  <h2>Information you send us</h2>
  <p>If you email us or use the contact form, we receive your name, email address and message. We use them only to reply and to fix any problem you report. We do not sell or share them.</p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>Like most websites, our hosting provider records basic technical data for each request, such as IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time. This is used for security and to keep the site running, and is kept only for a limited time.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>This site is intended to show ads served by Google AdSense and its advertising partners. <strong>The ad code is not loaded until you click Accept on the cookie message.</strong> If you click Reject, or make no choice, no ad script is requested and no advertising cookies are set by this site. Your choice is saved in your browser (local storage) so you are not asked again. <button type="button" id="reopen-consent" class="underline text-brand cursor-pointer">Change your choice</button> (reload the page to apply a withdrawal of consent).</p>
  <p>If you accept, ads are shown, and:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
    <li>Google uses the DoubleClick advertising cookie (also called the DART cookie) on sites that use AdSense. It lets Google and its partners serve ads based on your visits to this site and others, and it is also used to measure ads and prevent fraud.</li>
    <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google's <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For more on how Google uses data from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>. Visitors everywhere, including the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, are asked for consent before any advertising cookies are used.</p>

  <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p><strong>EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland (GDPR):</strong> the legal basis for advertising cookies is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time. You may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to the processing of your personal data, to receive a copy of it, and to complain to your data protection authority.</p>
  <p><strong>California and other US states (CCPA/CPRA and similar laws):</strong> you may have the right to know what personal information is collected about you, to request its deletion or correction, and to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information for targeted advertising. Choosing Reject on the cookie message keeps advertising cookies off.</p>
  <p>To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will answer within 30 days and will not treat you differently for exercising these rights.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. Its trivia is written for a general adult audience, and anyone under 13 should use it with a parent or teacher.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Pages may link to other websites, such as the data sources we cite. Their privacy practices are their own.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>When this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes too.</p>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var b = document.getElementById("reopen-consent");
      if (!b) return;
      b.addEventListener("click", function () {
        try { localStorage.removeItem("triviaquestionsdigest_consent_accepted"); } catch (e) {}
        window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("triviaquestionsdigest:reopen-consent"));
      });
    })();
  </script>
</PageLayout>
